  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the numbers be $a-5 d t, a-3 d, a-d, a+d, a+3 d, a+5 d$\r\nAlso, given $T_{1}=4 T_{3},$ where $T_{1}, T_{3}$ are respectively, first and third terms of AP. $\\Rightarrow \\quad a-5 d=4(a-d)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad d=-3 a=-\\frac{3}{2}$\r\n$\\therefore$ The fifth term $a+3 d=\\frac{1}{2}+3\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{9}{2}=-4$",
